  {
   "title": "QLC+ input profile M-VAVE-SMC-Mixer.qxi (non-official)",
   "url": "https://github.com/mcallegari/qlcplus/blob/6ed78ed0a697aaa48b1428271e004b22327e5be3/resources/inputprofiles/M-VAVE-SMC-Mixer.qxi",
   "note": "community profile by Massimo Callegari; Apache-2.0; numbers read from QLC+ channel numbers, not checked by this project",
   "license": "Apache-2.0"
  },
  {
   "title": "M-VAVE SMC-Mixer user manual",
   "url": "https://www.m-vave.com/download.html",
   "note": "manufacturer manual: SHIFT + ◁ / ▷ switches DAW / user mode; in DAW mode M, S, R and □ are mute, solo, record and select, and the light bar under each encoder blinks while a fader does not match the track volume"
  }
 ],
 "notes": "In DAW (Mackie) mode, which SHIFT + ◁ selects (SHIFT + ▷ goes back to user mode). Converted from the QLC+ community profile (Apache-2.0, see NOTICE); the faceplate, the labels from the manual (□ is Select, II is Stop, « and » are Bank − and +), the LEDs and most of these notes come from jcguevarap and his unit (firmware V012), PR #9. He checked that unit twice (issue #7), and both sittings are in verifications: on 2026-11-23 with a MIDI monitor, every control and its light; on 2026-11-24 with the verification page, every control but encoders 2–8, which it skipped because the file had them as buttons. The 52 controls the page confirmed are marked checked on hardware. Encoders 2–8 send CC 17–23 on the monitor reading and stay unconfirmed until a run on the page turns them. Every message number is the one QLC+ lists; the correction is the encoders: all eight are relative with a sign bit (1 = clockwise, 65 = counter-clockwise), where QLC+ has encoder 1 as absolute and 2–8 as buttons. The lights, as the owner reports them (this project has not checked them): the 32 strip buttons and Play, Stop, Record, Rewind and Forward light up with a Note On on the same note sent back to the unit (velocity > 0 on, 0 off; there is no blink). Bank −/+ and the arrows have no controllable light. The light bar under each encoder is not a ring: it does not answer the Mackie ring CCs 48–55; it is the unit's own soft-takeover indicator and blinks while a fixed Pitch Bend value sent to a fader differs from where the fader is. Faders have no motor and send Pitch Bend from −8192 to +8064 in steps of 128; the unit does not report their position until they move. The unit opens two input ports that repeat the same messages (\"SMC-Mixer\" and \"MIDIIN2 (SMC-Mixer)\"); the pattern picks the first. In user mode (as shipped) the messages are different: faders CC 0–7 on channel 1, encoders CC 0–7 on channel 3 (absolute), and the buttons switch their own lights.",
